msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:220
#: 1afb02e46cb74fc696a550de74018539
msgid ""
"First, make sure that ``qubes-windows-tools`` is installed in your system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:222
#: 4bf4696593dc463db8cf8d6f40110675
msgid ""
"For use with **Windows 7**, install the previous version of Qubes Windows "
"Tools. The corresponding .rpm file for manual QWT installation for Windows "
"7is still available from the repositories for Qubes R4.2 (version `4.1.69-1 "
"<https://yum.qubes-os.org/r4.2/current/dom0/fc37/rpm/qubes-windows-"
"tools-4.1.69-1.fc37.noarch.rpm>`__ )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:224
#: 8a81bfd7b41a40e1964eb00aaa5a2404
msgid ""
"After downloading, copy the file to `dom0` as described in `How to copy from "
"dom0 <https://www.qubes-os.org/doc/how-to-copy-from-dom0/#copying-to-"
"dom0>`__ and install it via ``sudo dnf install PATH_TO_RPMFILE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:226
#: ca0e89f0c5e641518d87c2ccd36a581a
msgid ""
"For use with **Windows 10 and 11**, you have to install the new version "
"4.2.2 of Qubes Windows Tools. In Qubes R4.3, the QWT package is already part "
"of the repositories. So, QWT can be installed directy, without downloading "
"anything, via"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:233
#: b314a7d822794f219034062a6ce91ee5
msgid ""
"**Caution:** Installing one of these QWT versions will remove the other if "
"it is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:235
#: f0e601bc06a1463d953be6e15a13b62d
msgid ""
"**Warning:** In Windows 7, the older version of Qubes Windows Tools will be "
"replaced during the next ``dom0`` update by the current dummy version "
"4.1.70-1. This can be inhibited by appending the line ``exclude=qubes-"
"windows-tools`` to the file ``/etc/dnf/dnf.conf`` in ``dom0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:237
#: b34b31e748ed459a937578a0a961788b
msgid ""
"This package makes the ISO with Qubes Windows Tools available, which is "
"passed to the VM when ``--install-windows-tools`` is specified for the ``qvm-"
"start`` command. Please note that none of this software ever runs in "
"``dom0`` or any other part of the system except for the Windows AppVM in "
"which it is to be installed. (It could not run in ``dom0`` at all, because "
"``dom0`` is a VM running under Fedora, while the QWT software is Windows "
"software.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:239
#: fadbe071dded43afad661e97c416b47a
msgid ""
"To install the Qubes Windows Tools in a Windows VM, one should start the VM "
"passing the additional option ``--install-windows-tools``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:245
#: 905864ecbaef41e1b75d87aae85bd185
msgid ""
"Once the Windows VM boots, a CDROM should appear in the ‘My Computer’ menu "
"(typically as ``D:`` or ``E:``) with the setup program with the setup "
"program ``qubes-tools-x64.msi`` for Windows 7 or ``qubes-tools-4.2.2.exe`` "
"for Windows 10 and 11 in its main directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:247
#: 3f74f6e9c039493cbb67299f529c2bf9
